# Iridium coverage hexagon: the patch of Earth one satellite can see.
# This file is shared by every satellite of the fleet; the demo rotates
# it so local +z points at the satellite, which puts it on the ground
# below.
#
#   footprint   psi = acos(R cos e / (R + H)) - e, for H = 780 km and the
#               8.2 degree elevation receivers need: psi = 19.9 deg,
#               4433 km across the circle
#   hexagon     regular, circumscribing that circle: corners at 23.0 deg,
#               4433 km across the flats, 5119 km corner to corner
#   surface     a spherical cap tessellated into 792 triangles and built
#               at radius 10.016, 10.19 km above the sphere of radius 10, so
#               every chord of the tessellation clears the globe (the
#               generator asserts it)
#
# Coordinates are bpp scene units: 1 unit = 637.1 km, north up; the mesh
# is centred on the scene origin, the Earth's centre, so a rotation is
# all it takes to place it -- no translation (see demo/koppi/iridium.lua).
#
# Faces are triangles, each corner carrying its face's own normal (out of
# the sphere); no texture coordinates, the tint comes from the object.
